  "description": "Light enters through the cornea and pupil, the lens focuses it, and the image lands upside down on the retina, where about 120 million rods and 6 million cones (of three types) turn it into signals. The optic nerve carries it to the brain, which flips it, fills in the blind spot and erases the jumps your eyes make about three times a second. Simplified original 3D animation; not medical advice.",
